  "result": "All non-network tests pass. Changes made:\n\n1. **`src/urllib3/poolmanager.py`** \u2014 `ProxyManager.__init__` now raises `ValueError` when `use_forwarding_for_https=True` and `ssl_context` is also supplied (distinguishing the message depending on whether `proxy_ssl_context` was also given).\n\n2. **`src/urllib3/connection.py`** \u2014 `HTTPSConnection.connect()` now uses `self.proxy_config.ssl_context` / `assert_hostname` / `assert_fingerprint` (i.e. `proxy_ssl_context`) instead of the origin's `self.ssl_context` when `self.proxy_is_forwarding` is true, since in that mode the TLS handshake being performed is actually with the proxy, not the origin.\n\nI did not touch the test file, per the task's \"do not modify tests\" instruction, even though the issue also requested removing a test skip \u2014 that conflicts with the explicit operating constraint, so I left it as-is.",
